  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 9,
    "tagline": "Week 9 News · Upsets · Survival · Central Chaos · Week 10 Pressure",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 9",
    "headline": "THE LEADERS FELL. THE BOTTOM FOUGHT BACK. WEEK 9 BLEW THE DOORS OPEN.",
    "deck": "Redwood and Sullco both went down, Flint finally turned a strong score into a win, Off Boys forced their way back into the conversation, and the Central delivered the two highest totals of the week in a 1.28-point knife fight.",
    "story": [
      "Week 9 did not respect the standings. Simpson Sith handed Redwood Murder its second loss, 96.60-84.40, while Off Boys knocked off East leader Sullco MethMouths 117.74-92.54. The two division leaders entered the week at a combined 13-3 and both left with a reminder that the stretch run will not be orderly.",
      "Off Boys produced the loudest statement from the middle of the pack. Puka Nacua led the way with 28.0 points, Bryce Young added 20.34, and Kyle rolled to a 25.20-point win over Sullco. At 4-5, the record is still below water, but the scoring profile has kept warning the league that this team is more dangerous than its place in the standings.",
      "The Central saved the finish of the week for last. Flint Tropics scored a league-best 118.76 and barely escaped THE Barton Spartans, 118.76-117.48. CeeDee Lamb, Bucky Irving, and the San Francisco defense powered Flint, while Christian McCaffrey, Jayden Coleman, and Patrick Mahomes nearly stole it for Barton. After weeks of good scores turning into losses, Stephen finally got the bounce.",
      "Medford MountainMen continued the late-season recovery with a 110.98-80.88 win over Your Mom. Christian Watson and Ja’Marr Chase combined for 53.10 points, giving Doug a second straight win and a third consecutive score above 110. The season record remains difficult, but the MountainMen are no longer playing like a bottom-tier team.",
      "Turbulent Ticklesh!ts stayed in control of the Central by beating Space Cadets 107.96-99.98, and California Un-Named Team handled Eskimo Brothers 109.94-91.72. Tyler keeps winning with the league’s strongest overall scoring profile, while Tavis moved to 7-2 and kept direct pressure on Redwood in the West."
    ],
    "awards": [
      {
        "emoji": "🔥",
        "title": "High Points, Finally Rewarded",
        "team": "Flint Tropics",
        "detail": "118.76 points, the best score of Week 9, and a win by only 1.28. After repeatedly wasting competitive totals, Flint finally converted one."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "💥",
        "title": "Statement Win",
        "team": "Off Boys",
        "detail": "117.74 points and a 25.20-point takedown of the East leader. Kyle moved to 4-5 and made the remaining schedule less comfortable for everybody."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "⛰️",
        "title": "The Mountain Is Moving",
        "team": "Medford MountainMen",
        "detail": "110.98 points and a 30.10-point win, the widest margin of Week 9. Medford has now cleared 110 in three straight weeks."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🎯",
        "title": "Nail-Biter of the Week",
        "team": "Flint Tropics vs. THE Barton Spartans",
        "detail": "A 118.76-117.48 finish decided by 1.28 points. Barton posted the second-highest total of the week and still lost."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "⚔️",
        "title": "Original Member Ambush",
        "team": "Simpson Sith",
        "detail": "Simpson dropped Redwood to 7-2 with a 96.60-84.40 rivalry win, tightening the West race without even being part of it."
      }
    ],
    "tidbits": [
      "Flint earned Week 9 high points at 118.76; the season Golden High Point remains Ticklesh!ts at 156.32 in Week 4.",
      "Barton scored 117.48, the second-highest total of the week, and lost. Your Mom scored 80.88, the week’s low total, and lost by the widest margin.",
      "Medford has scored 112.30, 121.00, and 110.98 over the last three weeks, a 114.76 average.",
      "Off Boys moved to 4-5 after beating the 6-2 East leader by 25.20 points.",
      "Redwood and California are now both 7-2, putting the West race under immediate pressure.",
      "Ticklesh!ts reached 6-3 and remains the Central leader after holding off Space Cadets by 7.98.",
      "Flint’s 1.28-point win was the closest game of Week 9; Medford’s 30.10-point win was the largest."
    ],
    "playoffTitle": "Five Weeks Left · The Margin Is Gone",
    "playoffInsights": [
      "East — Sullco remains first at 6-3, but Simpson improved to 5-4 and is now one game back. Space Cadets and Your Mom both fell to 3-6.",
      "West — Redwood and California are tied at 7-2. Eskimo Brothers sits at 5-4, while Off Boys improved to 4-5 and continues to carry spoiler potential.",
      "Central — Ticklesh!ts leads at 6-3. Medford and Flint both won, and Barton scored 117.48 in defeat. The standings still favor Tyler, but the division’s weekly scoring remains volatile.",
      "With five regular-season weeks remaining, Week 10 brings direct pressure games across all three divisions."
    ],
